# Everything is stored and checked out with LF, whatever the machine.
#
# The Windows sibling of this project keeps its C# files in CRLF, because its
# .editorconfig asks for it and `dotnet format` checks it in CI. Here the rule
# is the opposite, for the same reason: .editorconfig says LF, CI verifies it
# on a Linux runner, and a clone made on Windows with core.autocrlf=true must
# not hand the formatter CRLF files that would fail on the runner while looking
# fine locally.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must stay LF even on a Windows checkout: a CR at the end of
# the shebang line makes the kernel look for an interpreter called "bash\r".
*.sh        text eol=lf

# Binaries: no conversion.
*.png       binary
*.ico       binary
*.bin       binary
*.wav       binary
*.onnx      binary
